     "result_text_tail": "h Zipcart's fee and promotion cut added. I left it as written.\n\n**Choices I made for you:**\n- **Navy theme.**\n- **Source slide 14 split into pages 14\u201315.** The chart, table and three notes couldn't be read on one page, so every later page number moves up by one.\n- **Executive summary shortened** to five items, with the board decisions as item 5. Everything I cut from it is still in the body pages.\n- **Hypothesis slide placed under the market item.** Every content page has to sit under an executive summary item, and this one has no section of its own. It shows no section tracker, as in the source.\n- **No \"next steps\" end page,** because page 18 already lists the four decisions.\n- **Cover shows \"January 2027\" only,** since neither file gives a day.\n- I dropped one phrase from slide 7 (\"the two drivers it stretches furthest\"), because the plan actually stretches density the most.\n\n**Things you'll notice:**\n- In tables and sidebars, per-order amounts in cents are typed text, because the renderer would round them to one decimal ($6.17 would show as $6.2). So those workbook page sheets show fewer numbers, but each figure is checked against a data point and appears as a live formula on the Calculations sheet.\n- The 19 remaining check warnings are judgement items I reviewed and left: some sidebar figures aren't taken from that page's chart, a few pages are dense, and the growth rate's cube root can't be a live formula.\n\nIf you want, I can switch the theme or re-merge pages 14 and 15."
